ge_id="Idf24b4cda4f32db31a92d6ae7a895fde4f6bad30" commit="a4ee4373dfe7dc042d9f28e935c076f176b568e3" commit_message="Revert &quot;security_Minijail0: Add test for session keyring&quot;  All lakitu builders are broken by this. go/lakitu-bots  This reverts commit 42a2b98245faf3c17eb85047a3b25378afcb56fc.  Change-Id: Idf24b4cda4f32db31a92d6ae7a895fde4f6bad30 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/450844 Commit-Ready: Daniel Wang &lt;wonderfly@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Daniel Wang &lt;wonderfly@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Chirantan Ekbote &lt;chirantan@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="450844" owner_email="wonderfly@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/44/450844/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I96bc8ea7952f2aad37cb9b36113939be235a1fbc" commit="faf5c31b03f408487a95c6c1ee4909ac1b292532" commit_message="Added attribute to control file for testtracker  Change-Id: I96bc8ea7952f2aad37cb9b36113939be235a1fbc Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/446584 Commit-Ready: Tom Turney &lt;tturney@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Tom Turney &lt;tturney@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Tom Turney &lt;tturney@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Bindu Mahadev &lt;bmahadev@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="446584" owner_email="tturney@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/84/446584/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I54bd866111b5c9b5738575f23757e0cbe4907ec4" commit="fe071e8a051571246b909558146bc606de0b615a" commit_message="cr50: enable utmi wakeups  We had disabled wakeups on the AP phy when we were running on gru, because the AP phy was not in use. We never changed that for reef, so UTMI wakeups were disabled even when the AP USB was supposed to be enabled. After Cr50 went to sleep any usb transactions would drop bits, because Cr50 wouldn't notice anything was happening until it woke up on one of the HOOK_TICK events.  This change reenables UTMI wakeups on boards with AP usb. It writes 1 to USB_PCGCCTL_STOPCLK. This makes the controller disable the PHY clock whenever it detects a usb suspend. When it resumes out of suspend, this bit has no effect.  BUG=b:35774906 BRANCH=cr50 TEST=Boot up reef. Wait until cr50 goes to sleep run 'usb_updater -f' and verify that it runs successfully. Make sure deep sleep still works  Change-Id: I54bd866111b5c9b5738575f23757e0cbe4907ec4 Signed-off-by: Mary Ruthven &lt;mruthven@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/448988 Reviewed-by: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="3" gerrit_number="448988" owner_email="mruthven@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/88/448988/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I08c75151e8b8e2aeaac76ae1151dcb1759d8c935" commit="451cca718e181a6706ee671ca67951406f87e321" commit_message="[autotest] Pass in HostInfoStore from TestBed to it's children  BUG=chromium:699188 BUG=chromium:678430 TEST=unittests, test_push passes.  Change-Id: I08c75151e8b8e2aeaac76ae1151dcb1759d8c935 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/450866 Commit-Ready: Prathmesh Prabhu &lt;pprabhu@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Prathmesh Prabhu &lt;pprabhu@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="450866" owner_email="pprabhu@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.